# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RSG Carrier Hub — environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the real values:
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored. NOTHING with a real secret should ever be committed.
# There are two groups of vars: BUILD-TIME (baked into the browser bundle by Vite)
# and RUNTIME (read by the Express server at request time).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── BUILD-TIME · Supabase (client) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Baked into the browser bundle by vite.config.ts. Both values are BROWSER-SAFE:
# the publishable key is designed to ship in client code and is protected by
# Row-Level Security. vite.config.ts also accepts the plain SUPABASE_* names.
#
# Project: rsg-infrastructure (ref wibscqhkvpijzqbhjphg)
# Get the publishable key from: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API keys
#   → "Publishable" (sb_publishable_...), or the legacy "anon"/public key.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://wibscqhkvpijzqbhjphg.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"

# ⚠️  NEVER put the Supabase service_role key here or anywhere in the frontend/git.
#     It is not needed to run the portal (RLS handles browser access). It is only
#     for out-of-band bulk admin / seed scripts, kept server-side out of this repo.


# ── RUNTIME · Supabase (server) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The service-role key powers every carrier endpoint: the box reads and writes the
# directory on the browser's behalf, so no user ever logs into Supabase. It stays
# on the tailnet-only box and is never sent to the client. Without it the carrier
# endpoints return 503.
# SUPABASE_URL=""                      # defaults to VITE_SUPABASE_URL above
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""


# ── RUNTIME · LLM for the grounded advisors (server) ──────────────────────────
# Carrier Hub owns its own LLM config. Set ONE api key; the base URL is optional
# (omit it for a direct OpenAI call, set it to point at a LiteLLM proxy). Without
# a key the app still runs — the advisors just report themselves unavailable.
#
# The legacy HERMES_OPENAI_* / LITELLM_* / OPENAI_* names are still read as a
# fallback so a running container survives the rename, but CARRIERHUB_* is the
# canonical set and the fallbacks will be dropped once deploys have moved over.
#
# API key — first non-empty of these is used:
CARRIERHUB_LLM_API_KEY="sk-or-litellm-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"
# HERMES_OPENAI_API_KEY=""   # legacy fallback
# LITELLM_API_KEY=""         # legacy fallback
# OPENAI_API_KEY=""          # legacy fallback
#
# Base URL — optional; leave blank for api.openai.com.
# CARRIERHUB_LLM_BASE_URL="https://<litellm-host>/v1"
#
# Model — optional; defaults to gpt-4.1-mini. The global fallback for every task.
# CARRIERHUB_LLM_MODEL="gpt-4.1-mini"
#
# Per-task model tiers. Each should be a LiteLLM *model group* name, so the
# underlying model can be re-pointed on the proxy without redeploying the app.
# Resolution per task: the task env → CARRIERHUB_LLM_MODEL → gpt-4.1-mini.
# Leave unset until the groups exist on the proxy — pointing at a group LiteLLM
# doesn't define will 404 every call.
#
#   desk    — Ask Carrier Desk. Grounded, conversational, large cached prefix.
#             The whole carrier directory rides in the system prompt, so this is
#             the highest-token path; a mid tier plus prompt caching beats a
#             cheap model here.
#   advisor — per-carrier and panel appetite advisors. Mid tier.
#   quick   — short, low-stakes completions. Cheapest tier that still reads well.
#
# CARRIERHUB_MODEL_DESK="rsg_desk_default"
# CARRIERHUB_MODEL_ADVISOR="rsg_advisor_default"
# CARRIERHUB_MODEL_QUICK="rsg_quick_default"


# ── RUNTIME · MCP door (server) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Carrier Hub exposes its own MCP endpoint at POST /mcp, with one tool per app
# function — the same surface /api/functions describes. Callers send
# `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
#
# This FAILS CLOSED: with no token set the endpoint refuses every call rather than
# serving the write tools (including delete_carrier) to anything that can reach
# the port. Generate one with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# CARRIERHUB_MCP_TOKEN=""


# ── Notes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# • The server listens on $PORT, default 3000.
# • NODE_ENV=production makes Express serve the built ./dist bundle; anything else
#   runs the Vite dev middleware. `npm run dev` uses dev mode.
# • GEMINI_API_KEY is no longer used — the advisors moved off Gemini to LiteLLM/OpenAI.
